<title>FRANCE: FRENCH HEALTH SPENDING RISES 0.2 PCT IN JUNE.</title>
<headline>FRENCH HEALTH SPENDING RISES 0.2 PCT IN JUNE.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Total French health care spending rose 0.2 percent month on month in June, giving a year-on-year rise of 0.7 percent, the CNAM national health insurance fund said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Health care spending excluding public hospitals was up 0.3 percent month on month in June and 1.5 percent year on year, the CNAM said.</p>
<p>In May total health spending rose 0.2 percent month on month, giving a year-on-year rise of 0.4 percent, the CNAM said on July 7.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
